{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact clean pushed head 906b0a9441ab52c8ccf8e86bb68cb2d0bcb9706b on request/novice-cli-usability, against request ad7c3eab and all seventeen exact-path artifacts. Independent verification on a clean detached checkout with the binary built and driven against this repository: gates re-run there and green — gofmt empty, go build, go vet, git diff --check, go test ./cmd/gs ./internal/statusview ./internal/workroom -count=1, internal/docset gate, full go test ./... -count=1 (35 packages ok). The seventeen-file diff is exactly the artifact set; main is an ancestor; publish is preserved in usage and help; docs/reference/gs/work.md is main plus seven inserted lines with the awaiting-merge lane intact; internal/workroom changes are render.go decoration and a test, fold.go untouched. All five bounded conditions hold at runtime: real help exits zero for the top level, help cmd and every subcommand with usage plus flags on stderr and unknown flags list the flag set and exit one; gs whoami reports the signing actor and its source with the local custody roster, and gs work refuses a missing or unprovisioned identity with the custody list, the --as/GITSEQ_ACTOR choice and a docs pointer rather than falling back; gs work, gs status, gs status --all and gs inspect print full canonical event ids (zero truncated ids across a 6002-line status --all), and a prefix or #N given to inspect is refused with the full-id guidance rather than resolved; gs state validates body.commit by git rev-parse --verify --end-of-options with the commit peel and exact-equality before signing; the named refusals (cross-author merge preflight, promise mismatch, dangling promise) carry a next step and docs pointer, pinned by tests. Two defects to fix before approval. ONE, the full-id protection on the workroom render surface is hollow: TestRenderedSurfacesNameEventsByNumberAndCanonicalID (internal/workroom/fold_test.go:3617) says it is mutation-sensitive by construction, but I replaced name() with short(event) in render.go and the whole package stayed green, because the golden fixture ids (e0 to e9, w3) are at most sixteen characters, where short() is the identity (render.go:240-245). workroom.RenderStatus is the production surface behind gs status --all (main.go:1907,1931), so this is the one of the three id surfaces with no regression guard; statusview (view_test.go:435-470, real-length ids, short forms forbidden) and gs work/inspect (query_test.go:209) are protected. Fix with a direct name() test on an id of seventeen or more characters, or a long-id golden event, and make the test's claim true. TWO, full object resolution is enforced on one of two artifact-filing paths: gs state calls validateArtifactCommit (main.go:508-511, 1112-1122) but batchCommand via runBatch and resolveBatchAct (main.go:1503, 1616, 1708) never does, so an artifact filed through gs batch with a short or symbolic commit still fails only at merge, which is the exact late-refusal the condition exists to remove. Route batch artifacts through the same validator and add the mirror of TestArtifactFilingRequiresFullCanonicalCommit for batch. Mutation evidence otherwise: stripping the next step from succession.go:491 fails TestMergePreflightRefusesACrossAuthorRetirementOutsideTheApprovedTree at succession_test.go:252. ARCHITECTURE: surface layer (cmd/gs) plus the two projection renderers; no fold, kernel or application contract change; docs updated on the same head. SECURITY: whoami discloses only actor names, public fingerprints, kind, roles, custody and retirement, nothing gs actors did not already show, and echoes the invoker's own --repo value rather than a resolved absolute path; commit resolution uses exec argv with --end-of-options ahead of the user string and a commit peel, no shell, refusing non-commits, and the unbounded echo of body.commit in the refusal is a local CLI reflecting its caller's own argument before any signing, so no boundary is crossed; refusal decoration appends fixed strings only; no new path signs as anything but --as; the help argv rewrite inserts only --help. SIMPLIFICATION, non-blocking: explainDecisionReason is duplicated verbatim in statusview/view.go:598 and workroom/render.go:230 with the same two strings appearing a third time in main.go:1812 — one exported helper in workroom would remove a drift risk; name() is likewise duplicated across the two renderers; the unknown-flag error prints twice (flag package then the gs prefix); help goes only to stderr so gs --help piped to a pager shows nothing, which matches the request wording but is worth a sentence in the docs. Fix the two defects in a successor head and I will re-review promptly.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f21afd771e970cfcd1076dfd4c3f5290378b406b","head":"906b0a9441ab52c8ccf8e86bb68cb2d0bcb9706b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:89a2e74344eaf5714e60a80ac7911e361b9437a9\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3083331fcacba13a18abc2bf812383068d93dcd5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}